    "v2": {
      "_readme": "See ../README.md for the full write-up. Everything under artMeta is this pass's fuller record (per-layer files/boxes, named landmarks with visibility+confidence, judge verdicts, known issues) \u2014 the runtime's Rig interface (src/rig.ts) only reads the sibling top-level keys above; nothing here is consumed by loadRig today.",
      "sourcePlate": "public/art/portraits/yuna-x2.png",
      "sourceSha256": "7427dc7fc4811782c00be3888dbca713d04c3755328b179da3bfc5e1fd371200",
      "commonLandmarkOrder": [
        "pupil_R",
        "noseTip",
        "philtrum",
        "mouthCorner_R",
        "lipUpper",
        "lipLower",
        "chin",
        "hairlineCenter"
      ],
      "commonLandmarkNote": "Only 8 of up to 31 named points are visible on *all four* keys at once (mostly centreline points \u2014 the profile key hides one whole side, and the far eye is occluded by hair on both q34 keys), so that is what keys[].landmarks carries, in this fixed order, for index-based correspondence across keys. The full named set per key, including occluded/not-visible points and their confidence, is in landmarks/<key>.json \u2014 read that for anything needing more than 8-point correspondence.",
